X-Comment: Placeholder maintainer/homepage until the project has public hosting.

Package: jewbuntu-core
Architecture: all
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: pciutils
Description: Jewbuntu core configuration, diagnostics and migrations
 Shared per-user settings (XDG, versioned schema, atomic writes, verified
 backups), the 'jewbuntu' command, the hardware doctor, the support matrix,
 and a per-user systemd unit that migrates settings as the user.
 .
 Contains no personal data. Removing the package never deletes user settings.

Package: jewbuntu-branding
Architecture: all
Depends: jewbuntu-core (= ${binary:Version}), python3 (>= 3.10), ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: pipewire-bin | pulseaudio-utils
Description: Jewbuntu wallpapers and 8-bit startup jingle
 Original Jewbuntu wallpapers (light and dark) and a short chiptune
 arrangement of the opening phrase of the traditional melody "Hava Nagila",
 played once per boot at graphical login. Honors mute and the user's on/off
 setting, never raises system volume, and fails silently without audio.

Package: jewbuntu-hebrew
Architecture: all
Depends: fonts-noto-core, fonts-culmus, fonts-sil-ezra, hunspell-he, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: language-pack-he, language-pack-gnome-he
Description: Jewbuntu Hebrew input, fonts and language support
 Adds English and Hebrew keyboard layouts as the default input sources,
 nikud-capable Hebrew fonts with a fontconfig preference for Hebrew text,
 and the Hebrew spell checker.

Package: jewbuntu-upgrade-tools
Architecture: all
Depends: jewbuntu-core (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: ubuntu-release-upgrader-core
Description: Jewbuntu upgrade readiness report and repository enrollment
 'jewbuntu upgrade-check' inspects the system before an Ubuntu release
 upgrade (support matrix, disk space, held or broken packages, third-party
 sources, settings) without changing anything. 'jewbuntu repo' re-enables the
 Jewbuntu APT suite matching the running Ubuntu release after an upgrade.

Package: jewbuntu-desktop
Architecture: all
Depends: jewbuntu-core (= ${binary:Version}),
         jewbuntu-branding (= ${binary:Version}),
         jewbuntu-hebrew (= ${binary:Version}),
         ubuntu-desktop-minimal,
         fonts-inter,
         ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: jewbuntu-upgrade-tools (= ${binary:Version}),
            jewbuntu-gnome (= ${binary:Version}),
            zenity
Description: Jewbuntu desktop (metapackage and Mac-inspired defaults)
 Selects the tested Jewbuntu desktop components on top of Ubuntu's own
 desktop, and sets Mac-inspired GNOME defaults (bottom dock, left window
 buttons, translucent rounded dock, Inter font, blue accent, Jewbuntu wallpaper)
 through a vendor settings override.
 Users' own settings always take precedence; 'jewbuntu defaults restore'
 resets only the keys Jewbuntu manages.

Package: jewbuntu-gnome
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Enhances: gnome-shell
Description: Jewbuntu GNOME Shell integration (Mac-style top bar)
 A small GNOME Shell extension that moves the clock to the right of the top
 bar and makes the bar translucent. It is declared only for tested GNOME
 Shell versions (currently 50); on any other version GNOME disables it and
 the stock Ubuntu top bar is used. Nothing else depends on it.
 .
 Later milestones add the Jewish calendar indicator here; calendar data and
 logic stay in a separate service so the desktop never depends on this.
